{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_7uahb7n5v6crrxr6ltlqcok5vli4kkmgmiawl7oimioyqw5hohna","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verification complete — the Rust translation matches the C byte-for-byte on every tested input. No divergences were found, so no Rust source changes were needed.**\n\nThe library is `stb_ds`'s hash-map/dynamic-array implementation plus the `hm_geti` driver: 16 exported symbols, 982 lines of C, 1453 lines of Rust.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| gate | result |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — `nm -D` diff | **empty**, 16/16 symbols; undefined imports are libc/unwinder only |\n| Phase B — every `CONFIGS.md` row (43) | **44 tests pass** (`phase_b.rs` 23, `phase_b2.rs` 21) |\n| binary stdout comparison | **N/A** — `CMakeLists.txt` builds only `add_library(SHARED)`; the equivalent driver `hm_geti` is compared via its seed-global side effect |\n| Phase C — every `ERRORS.md` row (43) | **34 tests pass** (`phase_c.rs` 31, `phase_c_abort.rs` 3) |\n| all feature combinations | no `[features]` table → one configuration; also passes under the `dev` profile with `overflow-checks` on |\n\n## Artifacts (in `translation/`)\n\n- `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md` (43 rows), `CONFIGS.md` (43 rows)\n- `tests/common/mod.rs` — loads **both** `.so`s via `libloading` and drives them through identical macro-equivalent consumer code\n- `tests/phase_b.rs`, `tests/phase_b2.rs`, `tests/phase_c.rs`, `tests/phase_c_abort.rs`\n- `verify.sh` — builds C + Rust, checks symbol parity, loops over feature combos\n\n## What the comparison actually covers\n\nPer *operation* (not per test): returned index/`temp` sentinel, full array header, full hash index (all thresholds, `slot_count_log2`, `used_count`, `tombstone_count`, `seed`, arena fields), **every bucket's complete `hash[8]`/`index[8]` arrays**, raw element bytes, and the `temp_key` string. Randomized with fixed splitmix64 seeds.\n\nNotable inputs exercised: siphash `d[3]<<24` int sign-extension at every `len%8`; `stbds_hash_string`'s signed-char promotion on bytes ≥ 0x80; the missing `temp_key` store in `hmput_key`'s wrap scan; table grow 8→1024 and shrink back; tombstone rebuild; non-zero `keyoffset`; all four `string.mode` arms plus out-of-range values (`256`→0, `-1`→255, `i32::MIN`→0); out-of-range `mode` enums (`2`, `7`, `1000`, `i32::MAX`, `-1`, `i32::MIN`); arena block saturation at `1<<20`.\n\nTwo abort paths were made observable via child-process status comparison rather than being written off as untestable:\n- **`ERRORS.md` row 17** — `mode >= 2` deleting a non-final element makes `hmdel_key`'s re-find hash the raw element bytes as a C string, so `assert(slot >= 0)` fires. Both libraries: **SIGABRT (6)**.\n- **row 27** — `stbds_arrfreef(NULL)` → `free((char*)NULL - 32)`. Both: **SIGSEGV (11)**.\n\nRows 16, 18 and 21 are asserts unreachable through the 16 exported symbols; they're covered indirectly by the per-operation bucket-array comparison, and that reasoning is written into `ERRORS.md` rather than left implicit.\n\nTwo test-harness bugs I hit and fixed (not library issues): pointer-identity comparison for `arrgrowf`'s early return (`realloc` can coincidentally return the same block, so the branch is now predicted from the pre-state), and `i32::MIN as u64` overflowing a PRNG seed under `debug-assertions`.\n\nOne caveat worth stating: on abort, C's `assert` prints a diagnostic to stderr while the Rust `abort()` is silent. Termination status is identical; only the stderr text differs."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":801,"cache_read_input_tokens":207059,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":801,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"42494262-643a-4b7c-9e37-ce4fb93d675e","uuid":"c6c8ba72-d2f9-497d-baab-35fd31b79cf6","timestamp":"